### =====================================================================
### appointMe - day14-attacks.http   (Day 14: attack your own system)
###
### Cast (all password: correct-horse-1; load the NEW scripts/dev-seed.sql first):
###   ALICE = OWNER of tenant 1 "Test Barber"   <- the ATTACKER
###   GUS   = OWNER of tenant 2 "Second Gym"    <- the VICTIM
###
### Victim data that Alice must never reach:
###   service 3 "Yoga Class", customer 3 "Zoe Gym", membership 3 (Bob @ tenant 2),
###   membership 4 (Gus), and the appointment Gus books in V1 below.
###
### An attack PASSES only if ALL THREE are true:
###   1) the status code is the expected one,
###   2) the response contains NO data from the other tenant,
###   3) nothing changed in the database (check with the SQL in the lesson).
### Write the real result of every attack in security-attacks.md.
### Tokens last 30 minutes. Sudden 401s => rerun SETUP.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Victim ids (tenant 2) - Alice does not belong there
@victimServiceId = 3
@victimCustomerId = 3
@victimStaffId = 3

### Alice's own ids (tenant 1)
@ownServiceId = 1
@ownCustomerId = 1
@ownStaffId = 2


### ======================================================================
### SETUP
### ======================================================================

### A1. Alice logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### A2. Alice selects tenant 1. EXPECT 200, OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### G1. Gus logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gus@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("gusUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### G2. Gus selects tenant 2. EXPECT 200, OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/2
Authorization: Bearer {{gusUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("gusToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### V1. Gus books an appointment in tenant 2 (the victim record). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{gusToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{victimStaffId}}, "customerId": {{victimCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{victimServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-24T09:00:00Z", "notes": "GUS SECRET NOTE" }

> {%
    client.global.set("victimApptId", response.body.id);
%}

### V2. Alice books her own appointment (the baseline). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{ownStaffId}}, "customerId": {{ownCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{ownServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-24T10:00:00Z", "notes": "alice note" }


### ======================================================================
### GROUP 1 - READ another tenant's record by id   (all EXPECT 404)
### ======================================================================

### ATK-01. Victim's service. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/{{victimServiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-02. Victim's customer. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{victimCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-03. Victim's appointment. EXPECT 404 (no "GUS SECRET NOTE" anywhere)
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{victimApptId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-04. BASELINE: an id that exists NOWHERE. EXPECT 404.
###        Compare with ATK-01: the two bodies must look the same except for the id
###        in the text. If an attacker can tell them apart, ids can be enumerated.
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}


### ======================================================================
### GROUP 2 - WRITE to another tenant's record   (all EXPECT 404, data unchanged)
### ======================================================================

### ATK-05. Update the victim's service. EXPECT 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/services/{{victimServiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "HACKED", "durationMinutes": 1, "price": 0.00, "active": false }

### ATK-06. Delete (deactivate) the victim's service. EXPECT 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/services/{{victimServiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-07. Update the victim's customer. EXPECT 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{victimCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "HACKED", "email": "hacked@example.com" }

### ATK-08. Delete the victim's customer. EXPECT 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{victimCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-09. Change the status of the victim's appointment. EXPECT 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{victimApptId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CANCELLED" }


### ======================================================================
### GROUP 3 - CROSS-TENANT REFERENCES when creating an appointment
### Alice is allowed to book, but tries to attach the VICTIM's data to her booking.
### (all EXPECT 404)
### ======================================================================

### ATK-10. Foreign customer. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{ownStaffId}}, "customerId": {{victimCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{ownServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-25T09:00:00Z" }

### ATK-11. Foreign service. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{ownStaffId}}, "customerId": {{ownCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{victimServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-25T09:00:00Z" }

### ATK-12. Foreign staff member (Bob's membership in tenant 2). EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{victimStaffId}}, "customerId": {{ownCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{ownServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-25T09:00:00Z" }

### ATK-13. All three foreign at once. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{victimStaffId}}, "customerId": {{victimCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{victimServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-25T09:00:00Z" }


### ======================================================================
### GROUP 4 - LISTS must never include another tenant's rows
### ======================================================================

### ATK-14. Services. EXPECT 200, NO "Yoga Class"
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-15. Search for the victim's customer by name. EXPECT 200, totalElements 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?name=zoe
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-16. Customers, biggest page allowed. EXPECT 200, NO "Zoe Gym"
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?size=100
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-17. Appointments for the whole month. EXPECT 200, ONLY Alice's, NO "GUS SECRET NOTE"
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-18. Team list. EXPECT 200, Alice and Bob (tenant 1) only, NOT Gus
GET {{baseUrl}}/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}


### ======================================================================
### GROUP 5 - SPOOFING the tenant: every place a client could "say" it
### ======================================================================

### ATK-19. Tenant in the query string. EXPECT 200, STILL tenant 1's services
GET {{baseUrl}}/services?tenantId=2
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### ATK-20. Tenant in a header. EXPECT 200, STILL tenant 1's services
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
X-Tenant-Id: 2

### ATK-21. Tenant in the JSON body of a create. EXPECT 201 (or 400 if unknown fields are
###        rejected). Either way the row lands in tenant 1. Check with the SQL in the lesson.
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": 2, "tenant": { "id": 2 }, "name": "Spoofed service", "durationMinutes": 10, "price": 1.00 }

### ATK-22. Select a business Alice does not belong to. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/2
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceUserToken}}


### ======================================================================
### GROUP 6 - TOKEN attacks
### Forge with the helper (needs a token printed by A2 / the console):
###   powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\forge-token.ps1 -Token "<aliceToken>" -Claim tenant_id -Value 2
###   powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\forge-token.ps1 -Token "<aliceToken>" -Claim role -Value OWNER
### Paste the LAST line it prints in place of the placeholder below.
### ======================================================================

### ATK-23. Alice's token with tenant_id changed to 2. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer PASTE.FORGED.TENANT.TOKEN

### ATK-24. Same idea on Bob's STAFF token with role changed to OWNER. EXPECT 401
###        (log Bob in first, or use any tenant token and change a claim)
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer PASTE.FORGED.ROLE.TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Forged owner", "durationMinutes": 10, "price": 1.00 }

### ATK-25. Unsigned token ("alg":"none") claiming to be tenant 2's owner. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIn0.eyJzdWIiOiIzIiwidGVuYW50X2lkIjoyLCJyb2xlIjoiT1dORVIifQ.

### ATK-26. A valid USER token (no business selected) on a business endpoint. EXPECT 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceUserToken}}

### ATK-27. No token at all. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
